I started this particular game over a year ago, as a challenge from my
husband to win without genociding any species. I normally take out hL;R
so soon that I hardly see them in the game, so this was more difficult.
But I wanted to win with a dwarf also, having never played that race
before (I won with a human Arc in a previous version).

Since tonight was the first time I played the game since July, I don't
remember many details, but I can say I ascended with six unused amulets
of life saving (I did use one up earlier, but I don't remember the
circumstances), +6 Grayswandir (dual-weaponed with +6 silver saber),
and Excalibur in my bag. Nurses and incubi helped boost my HP to 374,
and I ended with a -39 AC (silver dragon scale, helm of brilliance,
Hawaiian shirt, cloak of displacement, speed boots (-38 AC when I wore
levitation boots), gauntlets of dexterity - all +4 or +5 except the
levitation boots). I was nervous about the krakens and giant eels in
the moat around the Wizard tower, but the force bolt spell did a
surprisingly good job once I maxed my strength and traded gauntlets of
power for gauntlets of dexterity.

Rodney didn't bother me much; the two or so times the wand of death
didn't kill him, Grayswandir did in short order. The only summoned
nasty was Yeenoghu, and I was surprised how quickly Gray took him down.
The most annoying part after getting the Amulet was the constant
"mysterious force" teleports down in Gehennom; I guess I'm not used to
playing lawful characters.

Used up a last wish on a cursed scroll of gold detection (after I tried
to write one and realized I hadn't actually ID'd it yet), wrote two
more and found the endgame portals easily. Took Death out quickly on
Astral, never encountered Famine or Pestilence (thank god/dess!) at all
as the first altar I came upon was the right one.

